{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'command-heads|help-text|defn.*(make-session|create-state|eval-program|eval-line|rebuild-session|handle-command|format-error)|:pending-run' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '230,343p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '390,455p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '810,905p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"421:(def command-heads\n429:(def help-text\n633:(defn format-error\n942:(defn- make-session\n1040:(defn create-state\n1240:        :pending-run nil\n1357:       (contains? command-heads (first form))))\n2014:  \"Give up the shell's `:pending-run` (section 7.2, step 7, the abandoned\n2035:   (if-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n2056:               :pending-run nil)\n2080:    (let [parked (:pending-run state)\n2126:   `:pending-run`, and the prompt returns.  Nothing is wedged: another\n2136:             :pending-run (cond-> {:vm vm'\n2157:   or park it as `:pending-run`.  `state` is the round's starting state;\n2244:(defn- eval-program\n2484:(defn- rebuild-session\n2519:          :pending-run nil}))\n2559:(defn handle-command\n2595:      help [state help-text]\n2641:   after it stay retained, in order, on the new `:pending-run`.\"\n2648:      (:pending-run state) [(update-in state [:pending-run :pending-lines]\n2658:  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run`: serve the\n2669:  (let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n2684:            (fold-queued [(assoc st :vm vm'' :pending-run nil) text]\n2696:                                               :pending-run parked'))]\n2715:                                  :pending-run nil)\n2724:  \"One re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` without an input line --\n2743:   (if (:pending-run state)\n2767:        links (get-in state [:pending-run :links])\n2771:      (and (:progress? served) (:pending-run state))\n2786:  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` behind a typed\n2803:  (if (and (:pending-run state) (not (command-line? parsed)))\n2889:   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n               \"--telemetry-stream\" (recur (nnext args)\n                                           (update opts :rejected conj arg)\n                                           extra)\n               (recur (next args) (update opts :extra (fnil conj []) arg)\n                      extra))))\n         (if finalize (finalize opts extra) opts))))))\n\n\n(defn- release-store!\n  \"Release what a failed construction had already acquired: the\n   composition's transport state first (its boards, dials and socket), then\n   the store handle (a durable directory's exclusive lock), each exactly\n   once.  A cleanup never throws over the refusal that caused it, and never\n   replaces it.\"\n  [composition opened]\n  (let [close (:close! composition)\n        session (:session opened)]\n    (when (and close session)\n      (try (close session)\n           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n    (try ((or (:close-store! composition) store/close!)\n          (:index-store opened))\n         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn boot\n  \"Create the composition: one shell, one input medium, one cursor held only by\n   the step owner, and the host WebSocket adapter `(connect ...)` attaches\n   through.  A custody composition (:custody, yin.vm.ucf.compose) rides the\n   shell as data; the step owner below is the only thing that steps it.\n\n   `composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage composition\n   past the engine's own two stores.  When it names the parsed\n   `:index-store-spec` as one of its own (`:composition-spec?`), `:open`\n   opens it and answers the two values of the ownership split: `:index-store`,\n   the generic `dao.jing` handle the engine is constructed with, and\n   `:session`, the transport state the composition keeps and steps beside\n   the engine — never inside it.  What the engine additionally needs to\n   drive that store arrives as `:engine-inputs` of the same answer (a\n   prepared `:link-source`, the composition's `:host-modules`), so a\n   `(reset)` or a `(vm ...)` rebuild reconstructs a session that still\n   resolves signed names and still serves the composition's modules.\n\n   The engine value lands at `:repl`, where the driver and the endpoint\n   read it, and the composition's transport state at `:session`; there is\n   no third place a node could hide.  A construction that fails after the\n   store was opened releases what it acquired (`release-store!`) and\n   answers its own refusal.\n\n   `:admission` is the session's admission policy, by default `{}`: the\n   publisher key's own principal only.  It is apart from `:principals`: a\n   declared publisher is not a trusted one.\"\n  ([opts] (boot opts nil))\n  ([opts composition]\n   (let [spec (:index-store-spec opts)\n         open (:open composition)\n         composition-spec? (:composition-spec? composition)\n         comp-store (when (and open composition-spec?\n                               (composition-spec? spec))\n                      (open spec opts))\n         repl-inputs (cond-> (if comp-store\n                               (merge {:index-store (:index-store comp-store)\n                                       :recovery (:recovery comp-store)\n                                       :publication-policy\n                                       (:publication-policy comp-store)}\n                                      (:engine-inputs comp-store))\n                               {:index-store-spec spec})\n                       true (assoc :publisher-key (:publisher-key opts)\n                                   :principals (:principals opts)\n                                   :admission (:admission opts {})\n                                   :custody (:custody opts))\n                       (:vm-type opts) (assoc :vm-type (:vm-type opts)))\n         state (try\n                 (driver/create-state\n                   {:host (or (:adapter opts) (host/websocket))\n                    :repl (repl.frontends/create-state repl-inputs)})\n                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                   (when comp-store (release-store! composition comp-store))\n                   (throw e)))]\n     (cond-> (assoc state :composition composition)\n       (:session comp-store) (assoc :session (:session comp-store))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition session\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn session-of\n  \"The composition session this host state carries: the engine at `:repl`\n   beside the transport state its composition owns at `:session`, joined as\n   the one value every composition function takes\n   (`yin.shell.session/make`'s shape).  Nil when the host drives no\n   composition.\n\n   The two halves live apart in the host state because the driver and the\n   served endpoint read the engine at `:repl` and know nothing of a\n   session, while the composition reads both.  A node is never inside the\n   engine value, so nothing engine-side can step one, and nothing\n   composition-side has to guess which key a session hides its node under.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-some [transport (:session state)]\n    (assoc transport :engine (:repl state))))\n\n\n(defn with-session\n  \"The host state after one composition round: the engine back at `:repl`,\n   where the driver reads it, and the transport state carried beside it at\n   `:session`.\"\n  [state session]\n  (-> state\n      (assoc :repl (:engine session))\n      (assoc :session (dissoc session :engine))))\n\n\n\n(defn- composition-stopped?\n  \"True when the composition owes nothing at exit — no transport state, or\n   transport state whose own exit condition is met.  A host with no\n   composition owes nothing.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [stopped? (:stopped? (:composition state))]\n    (boolean (stopped? (session-of state)))\n    true))\n\n\n(defn- composition-refusal\n  \"The text that refused the composition's store after startup (a socket\n   that could not bind, a hydration that could not complete), or nil.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-some [refusal (:refusal (:composition state))]\n    (refusal (session-of state))))\n\n\n(defn- composition-admitting?\n  \"Whether the shell may evaluate: a composition with a hydration still\n   outstanding, or one whose hydration was refused, admits nothing, and\n   every typed line waits in the input medium.  A host with no composition\n   always admits.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [admitting? (:admitting? (:composition state))]\n    (boolean (admitting? (session-of state)))\n    true))\n\n\n(defn- composition-busy?\n  \"True while the composition owes the shell a line, which keeps the tick\n   owner at its base cadence.\"\n  [state]\n  (boolean (when-some [busy? (:busy? (:composition state))]\n             (busy? (session-of state)))))\n\n\n(defn- composition-close!\n  \"The bounded drain's last resort: whatever the composition still owes\n   after `stop!` and its budget of `step`s is asked for once more and not\n   awaited.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-some [close! (:close! (:composition state))]\n    (close! (session-of state))))\n\n\n(defn- composition-startup-lines\n  \"What the composition states at startup about the session it opened —\n   where it follows a published head, and whether one is installed yet —\n   or nothing for a host that carries no composition.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [lines (:startup-lines (:composition state))]\n    (vec (lines (session-of state)))\n    []))\n\n\n(def bind-all-host\n  \"`--port` listens on every interface: loopback and the machine's own IP.\"\n  \"0.0.0.0\")\n\n\n(defn pick-ip\n  \"The address to advertise among a machine's non-loopback IPv4 addresses:\n   the first private-network one (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16), since a\n   tunnel or VPN interface can list ahead of the LAN's; else the first;\n    state))\n\n\n(defn- custody-owed?\n  \"True while the shell's custody composition owes a control-plane\n   write (compose/owed-control-write?): a pending write keeps the tick\n   owner's cadence at the base interval, like the driver's own.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n    (compose/owed-control-write? c)\n    false))\n\n\n(defn step-all\n  \"One tick of the single step owner: the local shell first, then the served\n   endpoint, against the same shell value.  A storage composition's\n   transport state is stepped first (`composition-step`): its lines print\n   before the shell's, a hydration still outstanding leaves every typed\n   line waiting in the input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.\n   The custody control plane is stepped next, before the refusal and\n   admission branches, so renewals, pending releases and request retries\n   continue during hydration and past a refusal.  A `--port` process\n   serves one shared shell, as v1's atom made it: the driver evaluates this\n   tick's local\n   lines first, so a definition typed at the local prompt is already in the\n   shell the endpoint evaluates remote requests against in the same tick, and\n   the endpoint's shell (remote definitions included) is threaded back\n   before the next tick.  The custody program step follows the driver's own\n   step and precedes the endpoint's; once the shell has stopped it is\n   replaced by the stop latch, so no custody program call runs after\n   `:running?` turns false.  A run parked on a completion this tick's\n   transport step produced is re-checked once, before any typed line and\n   with no line of its own, by the composition's own re-check — which\n   serves the link and call media the engine parks on and translates the\n   events before they cross inward, so linker progress resumes a parked run\n   and its text prints after the composition's lines.  Returns\n   `[state server lines]`; the caller only prints.\"\n  [state server now]\n  (let [[state comp-lines events] (composition-step state now)\n        state (custody-control-step state)]\n    (cond\n      (composition-refusal state)\n      [(custody-stop (assoc state :running? false)) server comp-lines]\n\n      (not (composition-admitting? state))\n      [state server comp-lines]\n\n      :else\n      (let [[state rechecked] (composition-recheck state events)\n            comp-lines (cond-> comp-lines\n                         (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked))\n            stepped (driver/repl-step state now)\n            [stepped after-input] (if (and (nil? (get-in state [:repl :pending-run]))\n                                           (get-in stepped [:repl :pending-run])\n                                           (:recheck-after-input (:composition stepped))\n                                           (session-of stepped))\n                                    (let [[session text] ((:recheck-after-input (:composition stepped))\n                                                          (session-of stepped))]\n                                      [(with-session stepped session) text])\n                                    [stepped nil])\n            stepped (if (:running? stepped)\n                      (custody-program-step stepped)\n                      (custody-stop stepped))\n            [entries state'] (driver/take-outbox stepped)\n            server' (when server\n                      (serve/step (assoc-in server [:repl] (:repl state'))\n                                  now))\n            [server-entries server''] (if server'\n                                        (serve/take-outbox server')\n                                        [[] nil])\n            state'' (if server'' (assoc state' :repl (:repl server'')) state')]\n        [state'' server'' (cond-> (into comp-lines\n                                        (map entry-text)\n                                        (into (vec entries) server-entries))\n                            (seq after-input) (conj after-input))]))))\n\n\n(defn moved?\n  \"The tick owner's cadence bit, computed from this tick's own results: true\n   when there are lines to print, when the endpoint reports movement (a\n   woken probe, a published notice), or when either composition still owes a\n   write -- the shell's own, a storage composition's, or a custody\n   control-plane one.  A pending write\n   keeps cadence at the base interval; it must never wait out a backoff\n   ceiling.\"\n  [state server lines]\n  (boolean (or (seq lines)\n               (driver/pending-write? state)\n               (composition-busy? state)\n               (custody-owed? state)\n               (and server (serve/moved? server)))))\n\n\n(defn prompt-owed?\n  \"True when the operator is owed a fresh prompt after a tick: the tick\n   printed lines, or it consumed input that printed nothing (a silent\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,109p' src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc; sed -n '72,115p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '148,204p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '408,486p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '320,398p' src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc; rg -n 'op/eval|boot-server|connect' test/yin/repl/{serve,driver,main}* | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,109p' src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc; sed -n '72,115p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '148,204p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '408,486p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; sed -n '320,398p' src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc; rg -n 'op/eval|boot-server|connect' test/yin/repl/{serve,driver,main}* | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.adapter\n  \"A small, host-neutral bridge between a line-oriented Yin REPL and the\n   DaoStream RPC state machine.\n\n   This is deliberately not a replacement for `yin.repl`: it does not create a\n   socket, evaluate a form, print, own an atom, or invoke a callback.  A driver\n   owns the state returned here.  Local shell commands are emitted as data for\n   that driver to evaluate locally; every other input string becomes one\n   `:op/eval` request through the explicit RPC client state.\"\n  (:require #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn]\n               :clj [clojure.edn :as edn]\n               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]))\n\n\n(def eval-operation :op/eval)\n\n\n(def local-command-heads\n  \"Commands which retain the legacy REPL's local meaning when a remote RPC\n   client is present.  The adapter emits their original input; it does not\n   interpret or execute them.\"\n  #{'connect 'disconnect 'help 'quit 'repl-state})\n\n\n(def rejected-command-heads\n  \"Commands the REPL does not have.  `(telemetry)` is out in every form, so\n   the adapter names the rejection as an event rather than doing nothing locally\n   or sending the line to a remote evaluator that would report it as a missing\n   var.\"\n  #{'telemetry})\n\n\n(defn state\n  \"Create adapter state around explicit, caller-owned RPC client state.\n   `:events` is an unpublished outbox; use `take-events` to consume it once.\"\n  [rpc-state]\n  {:yin.repl.adapter/rpc rpc-state\n   :yin.repl.adapter/events []})\n\n\n(def init-state state)\n\n\n(defn eval-request\n  \"Construct the request value used for a non-local input.  Normal callers\n   use `submit-input`, which delegates id allocation and append handling to\n   RPC.\"\n  [id input]\n  (rpc/request-value id eval-operation [input]))\n\n\n(defn- read-forms\n  \"Read the line with a non-evaluating reader on every host.  Sniffing an input\n   line for a shell command must never run it; anything the data reader rejects\n   is ordinary source for the remote evaluator.\"\n  [input]\n  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n     :clj (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n     :cljs (reader/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))))\n\n\n(defn command-form\n  \"Exactly one well-formed shell-command form, otherwise nil.  Reader failures\n   intentionally mean remote input: ordinary language source must reach the\n   remote evaluator unchanged.\"\n  [input]\n  (when (string? input)\n    (try\n      (let [forms (read-forms input)\n            form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n        (when (and (seq? form) (symbol? (first form))) form))\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn- command-head\n  \"The head symbol of one well-formed shell-command form, otherwise nil.\"\n  [input]\n  (first (command-form input)))\n\n\n(defn local-command\n  \"Return the local command symbol for one well-formed local shell command,\n   otherwise nil.\"\n  [input]\n  (let [head (command-head input)]\n    (when (contains? local-command-heads head) head)))\n\n\n(defn rejected-command\n  \"Return the command symbol for one well-formed command this slice rejects,\n   otherwise nil.\"\n  [input]\n  (let [head (command-head input)]\n    (when (contains? rejected-command-heads head) head)))\n\n\n(defn- adapter-result\n  [outcome state & {:as extra}]\n  (merge {:yin.repl.adapter/outcome outcome\n          :yin.repl.adapter/state state}\n         extra))\n\n\n(defn- append-event\n  [state event]\n  (update state :yin.repl.adapter/events conj event))\n\n\n  (let [result (stream/cursor handle :dao.stream/oldest)]\n    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n      (:dao.stream/cursor result))))\n\n\n(defn create-state\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([{:keys [input input-cursor repl host]}]\n   (let [input (or input (create-input-medium!))]\n     {:repl (or repl (repl.frontends/create-state))\n      :input input\n      :input-cursor (or input-cursor (mint-cursor input))\n      :input-ledger :untried\n      ;; The host WebSocket adapter is composition data, injected once.  Nil is\n      ;; the honest answer in a build with no host socket package.\n      :host (or host (host/websocket))\n      :connection nil\n      :adapter nil\n      :queued []\n      :outstanding nil\n      :retrying nil\n      :outbox []\n      :last-tick nil\n      :running? true})))\n\n\n(defn submit-line!\n  \"Append one typed line to the input medium and return the append outcome.\n   This is the whole of a line producer's work.\"\n  [input line]\n  (stream/append! input {line-key line}))\n\n\n(defn take-outbox\n  \"Return `[entries next-state]`, clearing the publication outbox exactly once.\"\n  [state]\n  [(:outbox state) (assoc state :outbox [])])\n\n\n(defn attach-remote\n  [state adapter-state]\n  (assoc state :adapter adapter-state :queued [] :outstanding nil :retrying nil))\n\n\n                 (conj lines (get (:dao.stream/value result) line-key)))\n\n          :dao.stream/gap\n          (recur (dec remaining)\n                 (-> state\n                     (assoc :input-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result))\n                     (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n                              \";; input lost: typed lines were evicted before this step\"))\n                 lines)\n\n          :dao.stream/blocked\n          [(assoc state :input-ledger outcome) lines]\n\n          [(-> state\n               (assoc :input-ledger outcome)\n               (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n                        (str \";; input \" (name outcome))))\n           lines])))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Local and remote input\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- evaluate-locally\n  [state line]\n  (let [[repl text] (repl/eval-input (:repl state) line)]\n    (-> state\n        (assoc :repl repl)\n        (assoc :running? (boolean (:running? repl)))\n        (publish :yin.repl.driver/result text))))\n\n\n(defn- rpc-client\n  [state]\n  (get-in state [:adapter :yin.repl.adapter/rpc]))\n\n\n(defn- remote-terminal\n  [state]\n  (:terminal (rpc-client state)))\n\n\n(defn- remote-unsent?\n  \"True while the RPC client holds an allocated request it has not managed to\n   append.  That request, not the driver's own record of the line, is what owns\n   the request path: `rpc/request!` retries it and ignores any new operation.\"\n  [state]\n  (rpc/unsent? (rpc-client state)))\n\n\n(defn pending-write?\n  \"True while a remote write the operator is owed remains in flight: a\n   request awaiting its response, a line held for a full writer, or an\n   envelope the RPC client still retains. This is one half of the tick\n   owner's `moved?` — a pending write must never wait out a backoff ceiling,\n   so cadence stays at the base interval until it clears.\"\n      ;; encoded request, with the same id, is retried on a later step.\n      :yin.repl.adapter/pending-request\n      (assoc state :retrying line)\n\n      ;; Nothing was allocated or sent: the answer could land before the\n      ;; response cursor, so RPC holds the request until `poll!` mints it.\n      :yin.repl.adapter/cursor-pending\n      (hold state line)\n\n      (-> state\n          (assoc :retrying nil)\n          (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n                   (str \";; request not sent: \"\n                        (name (:yin.repl.adapter/outcome result))))))))\n\n\n(defn- handle-line\n  [state line]\n  (let [command (adapter/local-command line)]\n    (cond\n      ;; A shell that has quit evaluates nothing more.  Hosts append an\n      ;; end-of-input `(quit)` that a typed `(quit)` has already answered.\n      (not (:running? state)) state\n\n      (not (string? line))\n      (publish state :yin.repl.driver/diagnostic\n               (str \";; ignored non-string input: \"\n                    (pr-str (data/summarize line diagnostic-bounds))))\n\n      (str/blank? line) state\n\n      ;; Local control commands bypass the remote queue, so a stuck or slow\n      ;; remote request cannot trap the operator.\n      (= 'connect command) (connect-command state line)\n\n      (= 'disconnect command) (disconnect state)\n\n      (= 'repl-state command)\n      (cond-> (evaluate-locally state line)\n        (:connection state)\n        (publish :yin.repl.driver/result\n                 (repl/format-value (connect/summary (:connection state)))))\n\n      (and (remote-routed? state) (not command))\n      (cond\n        ;; A dropped or ended remote evaluates nothing.  The line was never\n        ;; sent, so it waits for an explicit reattachment decision.\n        (remote-terminal state)\n        (-> state\n            (update :queued conj line)\n            (publish :yin.repl.driver/notice\n                     \";; not connected: queued until (connect …) reattaches\"))\n\n        ;; `:unsent` is the RPC client's own retained envelope, and the\n        ;; authority on whether the request path is free: submitting here would\n        ;; resend it and discard this line.  `:retrying` is only the driver's\n        ;; record of which line that envelope carries.\n        (or (:outstanding state) (:retrying state) (remote-unsent? state))\n        (queue-line state line)\n\n        :else (submit-remote state line queue-line))\n\n      :else (evaluate-locally state line))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Remote completions\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- completion-text\n  [event]\n  (case (:yin.repl.adapter/event event)\n    :yin.repl.adapter/response\n    (if (contains? event :yin.repl.adapter/error)\n      (str \"Error: \" (repl/format-value (:yin.repl.adapter/error event)))\n      (let [value (:yin.repl.adapter/value event)]\n        (if (string? value) value (repl/format-value value))))\n\n    :yin.repl.adapter/lost\n        endpoint (cond-> endpoint\n                   (> (:gaps now-seen) (:gaps seen 0))\n                   (notice \";; endpoint lifecycle gap\"))\n        endpoint (reduce (fn [endpoint attachment]\n                           (notice endpoint (str \";; attachment \" attachment \" left\")))\n                         endpoint departed)]\n    (cond-> endpoint\n      (and changed? (= :refused (:status server)))\n      (notice (refused-text server))\n\n      (and changed? (= :stopped (:status server)))\n      (notice (stopped-text (get-in server [:stop :outcome]))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Requests\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- evaluate\n  \"Answer one validated request against the one shared shell, serially.\"\n  [repl request]\n  (let [id (rpc/request-id request)]\n    (cond\n      (not= eval-operation (rpc/request-op request))\n      [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/unknown-operation\n                              \"This endpoint answers :op/eval only; it does not proxy\")]\n\n      (not (string? (first (rpc/request-args request))))\n      [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/invalid-arguments\n                              \"An :op/eval request carries one source string\")]\n\n      :else\n      (try\n        (let [[repl' text] (repl/eval-input repl (first (rpc/request-args request)))]\n          (if (:pending-input repl')\n            ;; Line continuation is a terminal concern.  One shared shell means\n            ;; an unbalanced request would otherwise prefix the *next*\n            ;; caller's source, so the fragment is refused and dropped here\n            ;; rather than retained across a caller boundary.  The envelope\n            ;; was well formed, so the refusal is this server's decision and\n            ;; carries this server's code: a client can tell it from a codec\n            ;; defect.\n            [(assoc repl' :pending-input nil)\n             (rpc/error-answer id incomplete-input-code\n                               \"Incomplete input: a request carries one complete form\")]\n            [repl' (rpc/success-answer id text)]))\n        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n          [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/handler-error \"Handler failed\")])))))\n\n\n(defn- deliver-answer\n  \"Append one retained answer, advancing the requests cursor only when the\n   append is accepted.  `full` retries the identical answer on a later step\n   without re-running the handler.\"\n  [endpoint]\n  (let [result (stream/append! (:answers endpoint) (:pending-answer endpoint))\n        outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n    (case outcome\n      :dao.stream/ok\n      (assoc endpoint\n             :requests-cursor (:pending-successor endpoint)\n             :pending-answer nil\n             :pending-successor nil)\n\n      :dao.stream/full\n      endpoint\n\n      (-> endpoint\n          (assoc :requests-cursor (:pending-successor endpoint)\n                 :pending-answer nil\n                 :pending-successor nil)\n          (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n                   (str \";; answer undeliverable: \" (name outcome)))))))\n\n\n(defn- advance-requests\n  \"One bounded sweep of the shared requests/answers pair: a pending answer\n   is retried first (its retry runs on the host's cadence, gated on\n   nothing), then at most `request-budget` further request/answer cycles.\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:7:   `yin.repl.connect` client attaches through its `:connect!`, so the\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:14:   yin.repl.serve-connect-wire-test (JVM).\"\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:21:            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:56:(defn- connect!\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:143:      (testing \"a client connects over the bound URL and round-trips\"\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:144:        (let [[endpoint c now] (connect! host endpoint 2)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:145:              requested (rpc/request! @(:client c) :op/eval [\"(+ 1 2)\"])\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:225:        [endpoint c now] (connect! host endpoint 2)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:256:        [endpoint c now] (connect! host endpoint 2)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:260:    (swap! (:connection c) connect/close!)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:290:  (stream/append! (:requests endpoint) (rpc/request-value id :op/eval [source])))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:407:                    (rpc/request-value \"opaque-id\" :op/eval [\"(+ 1 2)\"]))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:439:    (testing \"a connected client is listed by its attachment\"\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:440:      (let [[endpoint _c _now] (connect! host endpoint 2)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:1:(ns yin.repl.serve-connect-wire-test\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:2:  \"The demo REPL flow over a real JVM WebSocket: `serve!` and `connect`\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:7:            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:38:                       \"serve-connect-wire-test\")\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:46:  \"Drive the connection's dial and poll its RPC client for a while before\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:53:  [connection adapter-state]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:56:      (swap! connection connect/step! (System/currentTimeMillis))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:70:  [connection adapter-state input]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:73:      (swap! connection connect/step! (System/currentTimeMillis))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:81:  [connection adapter-state]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:85:        (swap! connection connect/step! (System/currentTimeMillis))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:93:(deftest eval-round-trips-then-disconnect-and-reattach-over-a-real-socket\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:99:            opened (connect/open {:url url :host (host/websocket)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:101:        (is (= :yin.repl.connect/attached (get opened connect/outcome-key)))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:102:        (let [connection (atom (get opened connect/connection-key))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:103:              adapter-state (atom (adapter/state (get opened connect/client-key)))]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:104:          (is (= :established (:status @connection)))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:106:          (is (warm-up! connection adapter-state))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:107:          (is (submit-with-retry! connection adapter-state \"(+ 1 2)\"))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:108:          (let [events (poll-until-event! connection adapter-state)]\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:113:          (swap! connection connect/close!)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:116:                   (swap! connection connect/step! (System/currentTimeMillis))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:122:          (let [reattached (connect/reattach\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:123:                             @connection (:yin.repl.adapter/rpc @adapter-state)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:125:            (is (= :yin.repl.connect/reattached\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:126:                   (get reattached connect/outcome-key)))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:127:            (reset! connection (get reattached connect/connection-key))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:129:                   (get reattached connect/client-key)))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:130:          (is (= :established (:status @connection)))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:132:          (is (submit-with-retry! connection adapter-state \"(+ 40 2)\"))\ntest/yin/repl/serve_connect_wire_test.clj:133:          (let [events (poll-until-event! connection adapter-state)]\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:8:                :cljs [[yin.repl.connect :as connect]])\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:265:    (is (nil? (repl/boot-server (repl/parse-args []))))))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:634:  \"Append one `:op/eval` request directly onto the endpoint's requests\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:638:  (stream/append! (:requests server) (rpc/request-value id :op/eval [source])))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:647:        ;; Adoption is observed on the step after the connection reaches\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:687:;; is precisely that the served stream survives a connection's death: a\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1019:       \"Spawn B, wait for its bootstrap, and have it `(connect …)` exactly the\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1029:          (ask! peer {:cmd :line :line (str \"(connect \\\"\" (:url a) \"\\\")\")}\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1032:                                         #(= :yin.repl.connect/connected (:event %))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1053:        answered, and disconnect while it is outstanding.  Returns nil; the\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1060:       (ask! peer {:cmd :line :line \"(disconnect)\"} :line reply-ms))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1086:     (deftest ^:slow killing-the-connection-is-observable-and-requests-are-lost\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1102:               (is (= :detached (get-in probe-reply [:connection :status])))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1123:                 first-attachment (get-in before [:connection :attachment])]\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1131:               (ask! peer {:cmd :line :line (str \"(connect \\\"\" (:url a) \"\\\")\")}\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1134:                                       #(= :yin.repl.connect/connected (:event %))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1143:                           (get-in after [:connection :attachment]))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1165:                                         #(= :yin.repl.connect/ended (:event %))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1170:                                 #(= :yin.repl.connect/detached (:event %))))\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:1174:                   (is (= :ended (get-in probe-reply [:connection :status])))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short --branch; rg --files --hidden src/cljc/yin test/yin collab -g AGENTS.md; sed -n '150,225p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '1,143p' test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn|deftest' test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short --branch; rg --files --hidden src/cljc/yin test/yin collab -g AGENTS.md; sed -n '150,225p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '1,143p' test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn|deftest' test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"## store-swap-p1...origin/master\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795360785000-architect-store-swap-design.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795361680000-engineer-store-swap-p1.gpt-6.2-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795361680000-engineer-store-swap-p1.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/AGENTS.md\n(ns yin.repl.store-test\n  \"The index store's startup selection and durable lifecycle\n   (yin.repl.store): the default is the in-memory store today's shell\n   uses, `file:<dir>` opens `<dir>/content.jing` under an exclusive\n   directory lock, publishes each round's manifest address to a versioned\n   `<dir>/HEAD` through an atomic temp/sync/rename replacement, and\n   refuses every invalid spec or corrupt durable state — a missing value,\n   an unknown scheme, an empty or unopenable directory, a host without\n   file support, a handle and a spec together, a malformed HEAD, a\n   missing manifest, an unreadable index node — with its reason, never\n   answered with a silent memory fallback.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:core\" :as dart-core] [\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n                       [\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]\n                       [clojure.edn :as edn]])\n            #?(:cljd nil\n               :clj [clojure.edn :as edn]\n               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n            [clojure.set :as cset]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.datom :as datom]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.file :as dao.jing.file]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as jing.mem]\n            [dao.space.index :as dao.index]\n            [dao.space.transactor :as transactor]\n            [dao.stream :as dao.stream]\n            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n            [dao.space.store :as durable]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.fixture :as fixture]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Host helpers — a scratch directory, a scratch file, and their cleanup.\n;; These are the only host-aware lines in the suite.\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- temp-dir\n  []\n  (str \"target/test-index-store-\" (random-uuid)))\n\n\n(defn- temp-file\n  []\n  (str \"target/test-index-blocker-\" (random-uuid) \".tmp\"))\n\n\n(defn- write-file!\n  [path]\n  #?(:cljd (let [f (dart-io/File. path)]\n             (when-not (.existsSync (.-parent f))\n               (.createSync (.-parent f) .recursive true))\n             (.writeAsStringSync f \"\"))\n     :clj (do (.mkdirs (.getParentFile (java.io.File. path)))\n              (spit path \"\"))\n     :cljs (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")\n                 path-module (js/require \"path\")]\n             (.mkdirSync fs (.dirname path-module path) #js {:recursive true})\n             (.writeFileSync fs path \"\"))))\n\n\n(defn- cleanup-dir!\n  [dir]\n  #?(:cljd (try (.deleteSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n                (catch Object _ nil))\n     :clj (let [f (java.io.File. dir)]\n            (when (.isDirectory f)\n              (doseq [child (.listFiles f)]\n                (.delete child))\n              (.delete f)))\n     :cljs (try (.rmSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true :force true})\n                (catch :default _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn- cleanup-file!\n  [path]\n  #?(:cljd (try (let [f (dart-io/File. path)]\n                  (when (.existsSync f) (.deleteSync f)))\n                (catch Object _ nil))\n     :clj (let [f (java.io.File. path)]\n            (when (.exists f) (.delete f)))\n     :cljs (try (.unlinkSync (js/require \"fs\") path)\n                (catch :default _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn- refusal-of\n  \"The error `thunk` throws, or nil when it does not.  The error itself,\n   not its message: on the shadow-cljs test build, `(str (this-helper …))`\n   at an assertion site is compile-time evaluated and its constant\n   embedded, so a refusal's message would never be checked at runtime —\n   `(ex-message (refusal-of …))`, with the helper one level down, is the\n   shape that runs.\"\n  [thunk]\n  (try (thunk)\n       nil\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                 :clj Exception\n                 :cljs :default)\n              e\n         e)))\n\n\n(defn- read-text!\n  \"The file at `path` as text, or nil when absent.\"\n  [path]\n  #?(:cljd (let [f (dart-io/File. path)]\n             (when (.existsSync f) (.readAsStringSync f)))\n     :clj (let [f (java.io.File. path)]\n            (when (.exists f) (slurp f)))\n     :cljs (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")]\n             (when (.existsSync fs path)\n               (.readFileSync fs path \"utf8\")))))\n\n\n(defn- read-edn\n  [text]\n  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string text)\n     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n     :cljs (reader/read-string text)))\n\n\n(defn- head-path\n  [dir]\n  (str dir \"/HEAD\"))\n\n\n(defn- head-record-of\n  \"The parsed HEAD record of `dir`, or nil when absent.\"\n  [dir]\n  (some-> (read-text! (head-path dir)) read-edn))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Raw content-log surgery — the framed [4-byte length][frame] records of\n;; content.jing, read and rewritten as plain bytes per host, so a corrupt\n;; index can be fabricated the way a crash or a rotting disk makes it.\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- read-bytes!\n20:            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n42:(defn- temp-dir\n47:(defn- temp-file\n52:(defn- write-file!\n66:(defn- cleanup-dir!\n79:(defn- cleanup-file!\n90:(defn- refusal-of\n107:(defn- read-text!\n119:(defn- read-edn\n126:(defn- head-path\n131:(defn- head-record-of\n143:(defn- read-bytes!\n151:(defn- write-bytes!\n159:(defn- byte-count\n166:(defn- byte-at\n173:(defn- int32-at\n183:(defn- frame-starts\n192:(defn- splice-out!\n217:(defn- drop-frame-with-address!\n237:(defn- corrupt-payload-byte!\n253:(defn- write-text!\n267:(defn- absent-address\n274:(defn- hex-altered\n288:(defn- stream-values\n299:(defn- transactions\n309:(deftest the-flag-value-parses-to-a-spec-or-refuses-its-reason\n321:(deftest an-embedder-spec-is-checked-the-same-way\n338:(deftest the-default-is-the-in-memory-store-of-today\n346:(deftest a-host-without-file-support-is-refused-not-fallen-back\n360:(deftest an-unopenable-directory-is-refused-with-its-reason\n377:(deftest a-handle-and-a-spec-together-are-refused\n395:(deftest a-file-store-opens-content-jing-and-receives-publications\n427:(defn- durable-shell!\n433:(deftest a-durable-store-carries-its-lock-head-and-recovery\n458:(deftest a-second-owner-of-the-directory-is-refused-and-the-first-is-unaffected\n488:   (deftest a-real-second-jolt-process-is-refused-and-its-death-releases\n534:   (deftest a-real-second-jvm-process-is-refused-and-its-death-releases\n579:   (defn- claim-files\n588:   (defn- dead-pid\n596:   (deftest a-live-foreign-owner-is-refused-and-a-dead-ones-lock-is-replaced\n632:   (deftest a-concurrent-takeover-of-a-dead-owners-lock-leaves-one-owner\n666:   (deftest a-takeover-that-crashed-midway-does-not-brick-the-directory\n732:   (deftest two-worker-threads-of-one-process-never-both-own-the-directory\n776:   (deftest a-short-write-never-becomes-a-partial-head\n804:(defn- set-dir-readable!\n814:(deftest a-failed-directory-sync-fails-the-head-replacement\n834:(deftest a-round-whose-head-cannot-be-made-durable-is-not-published\n852:(deftest an-unreadable-node-in-any-index-refuses-startup\n875:(deftest a-failing-content-close-still-releases-the-lock\n891:   (deftest a-real-second-dart-process-is-refused-and-its-death-releases\n937:(defn- make-read-only!\n947:(deftest head-replacement-is-a-rename-of-a-synced-temp-never-a-partial-head\n977:(deftest a-publication-interrupted-before-the-rename-reopens-the-previous-snapshot\n1010:(deftest a-published-head-recovers-and-a-new-round-replaces-it\n1036:(deftest a-crash-before-the-rename-keeps-the-previous-snapshot\n1057:(deftest a-malformed-head-refuses-startup-and-leaks-no-lock\n1084:(deftest a-missing-manifest-refuses-startup\n1101:(deftest an-unreadable-index-node-refuses-startup\n1122:(deftest a-corrupt-content-log-refuses-startup\n1136:(deftest an-unreferenced-blob-after-a-crash-is-harmless\n1168:(defn- q-line\n1175:(defn- evaluate\n1184:(defn- provenance-line\n1196:(defn- provenance\n1203:(defn- local-datoms\n1209:(defn- ids-of\n1218:(deftest a-restarted-durable-shell-answers-q-with-the-previous-runs-facts\n1299:(deftest mem-mode-reset-still-starts-an-empty-index\n1316:(defn- memory-log!\n1331:(defn- publish-fixture!\n1359:(defn- groups\n1373:(deftest a-restart-restores-every-transaction-group-history-row-and-retraction\n1426:(deftest vm-selection-says-what-it-keeps\n1455:(defn- modulo-token\n1463:(deftest the-same-programs-publish-the-same-frontier-on-either-backend\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '942,1040p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1105,1254p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2244,2357p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '942,1040p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '1105,1254p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2244,2357p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- make-session\n  \"Build the evaluator, its media, their attachments and observers, the\n   expander, and the loader the evaluator observer feeds the VM, together.\n   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\n   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\n   lifetime.\n\n   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\n   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\n   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\n   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\n   which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\n   (`yin.repl.index`) is a peer attached to `program-out` beside it; the\n   round advances each, and neither calls the other.  It records\n   `shell-token` as provenance and publishes into `index-store`.  The AST\n   indexer (`yin.repl.ast-index`), holding the session's `$ast` and `$occ`\n   relations, is a third such peer.\n\n   The session owns one linker value. Its source configuration outlives\n   a session rebuild.\n\n   The query call pair is the session's too (`yin.repl.query/make-pair`):\n   the VM's half is its FFI pair, the interpreter's half with its request\n   cursor sits under `:query-pair`, and the interpreter answers from the\n   session's `:indexer`, and `:ast-indexer` for `$ast` and `$occ`, as they\n   stand when it serves.\n\n   A durable store's HEAD write is the composition's, reached over the\n   publication medium pair (`yin.repl.publication`): every session the\n   store outlives publishes through the same one.\n\n   `publication` carries that medium pair beside the composition's\n   immutable generic publication policy — `:publication-policy`,\n   `{:branching-factor n :max-payload-bytes b}`, a nil byte ceiling\n   declaring none (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 5).\n   The policy the composition injected wins over one the store handle\n   declares; the indexer threads whichever it is given through the bulk,\n   incremental and restore publication paths alike, and no transport's\n   page size is hardcoded here.\n\n   `host-modules` is the composition's module registrations, installed\n   into every session's registry so a rebuild never drops them\n   (`make-vm`).\"\n  [vm-type output-stream extra-primitives shell-token index-store source\n   publication host-modules]\n  (let [linker (link/make source)\n        pair (:pair linker)\n        query-pair (query/make-pair query-pair-capacity)\n        vm (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives pair query-pair\n                    host-modules)\n        program-in (make-attachment ingress-capacity)\n        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\n    {:vm vm\n     :load-program (get program-loaders vm-type)\n     :program-stream (:stream program-in)\n     :program-identity (:identity program-in)\n     :observer (:observer program-in)\n     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n     :call-site-admissions {}\n     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n     :row-observer (:observer program-out)\n     :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\n                                   :session-token shell-token\n                                   :content-store index-store\n                                   :publication-policy\n                                   (or (:publication-policy publication)\n                                       (:publication-policy index-store)\n                                       (:publish-opts index-store))\n                                   :publication-media (:media publication)})\n     :ast-indexer (ast-index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))})\n     :linker linker\n     :query-pair (dissoc query-pair :out-cursor)}))\n\n\n(defn- checked-link-policy\n  \"Validate the `:link-policy` creation option, failing closed at\n   assembly (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3): `:manual` is the\n   default and today's behavior, a function `(fn [view])` is the\n   embedder's rule, and `:lease` is reserved for the phase-2 deadline --\n   refused, not implemented yet.  Anything else is refused with the\n   supported values named.\"\n  [policy]\n  (cond\n    (or (nil? policy) (= :manual policy)) :manual\n    (fn? policy) policy\n    :else\n    (throw\n      (ex-info\n        (if (= :lease policy)\n          \"Yin REPL :link-policy :lease is not implemented yet\"\n          \"Unknown Yin REPL :link-policy\")\n        {:link-policy policy\n         :supported [:manual :fn]}))))\n\n\n(declare selected-primitives)\n\n\n(defn create-state\n   every publication path it takes (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md\n   section 5) — and the link source it drives as\n   `:link-source`.  The engine steps no transport and holds no node: a\n   round publishes against the injected handle and never waits on a\n   network, and a link the engine cannot serve itself stays pending for\n   its composition to move (`yin.shell.linker/serve-links`).  Supplied\n   together, `:link-source` wins over the generic content options, and\n   `:index-store` wins over `:index-store-spec`.\n\n   `:principals` are the public keys whose signed name assertions the\n   reader honors, and `:follow` the principal ids whose published heads\n   the composition follows.  Both are plain data on the link source; a\n   `(require ...)` of a name that is absent while a followed principal\n   has no installed head stays pending until that head is installed.\n   `:publisher-key` is the session's own signing key `{:seed :public}`,\n   whose principal joins `:principals` and is the `:own` the trust\n   commands always honor.  It is signing material, not transport state:\n   the engine reads only the principal off it, and never signs, resolves\n   or announces.  A prepared `:link-source` already carries all three, so\n   it wins and these are not read.\n\n   `:custody` is an optional custody composition value\n   (yin.vm.ucf.compose): the shell only carries it, as data, so the\n   host's single step owner can advance it (yin.repl.main/step-all --\n   the custody control step runs during hydration and through the\n   bounded shutdown drain; the custody program step runs only while\n   the shell is admitted and running).  Nothing in the shell reads or\n   steps it; nil, the default, is today's behaviour.\n\n   `:frontends` is the frontend catalog (`yang.frontend`) the session\n   compiles through, composed by the host entry point (this namespace\n   requires no frontend; see `yin.repl.frontends`).  Without it the catalog\n   is empty and every compile answers `unavailable-parser`.  The session\n   pins this immutable snapshot: installing into another catalog value\n   never changes a live session.  `:lang` selects a frontend by id\n   (`:yang/python`) or by `[id revision]`; a language keyword is not a\n   selector. The default is the `:yang/clojure` frontend.\n   one the catalog cannot answer is an `unavailable-parser` diagnostic,\n   never a fallback to another frontend.\"\n  ([] (create-state {}))\n  ([{:keys [lang output-cursor output-stream vm-type primitives\n            content-store content-client name-env link-policy index-store\n            index-store-spec link-source recovery principals follow custody\n            frontends admission publication-policy publication-media\n            host-modules publisher-key]\n     :or {lang :yang/clojure vm-type :semantic admission {}}}]\n   (let [output-stream (or output-stream (make-output-medium!))\n         output-cursor (or output-cursor (mint-cursor output-stream))\n         shell-token (str (random-uuid))\n         index-store-spec (cond\n                            (and index-store index-store-spec)\n                            (throw (ex-info\n                                     (str \"yin.repl/create-state takes one \"\n                                          \"index store: :index-store-spec \"\n                                          \"(mem or a file directory) or \"\n                                          \":index-store (a dao.jing handle), \"\n                                          \"not both\")\n                                     {:index-store-spec index-store-spec}))\n\n                            index-store nil\n\n                            :else (store/checked-spec index-store-spec))\n         ;; A composition that owns a storage implementation prepares the\n         ;; link source beside the handle and injects both; the engine\n         ;; composes one only from the generic content inputs it was given\n         ;; (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 3).  Composed\n         ;; before the store opens: a refused composition never holds a\n         ;; directory lock.\n         link-source (or link-source\n                         (link/composition\n                           {:name-env name-env\n                            :content-store content-store\n                            :content-client content-client\n                            :principals principals\n                            :key publisher-key\n                            :follow follow\n                            :admission (when-not (= :external admission)\n                                         admission)}))\n         index-store (or index-store (store/open index-store-spec))\n         recovery (or recovery (:recovery index-store))\n         ;; the composition's durable-publication medium: the engine\n         ;; emits a correlated request and promotes only the matching\n         ;; result, and its indexer holds no writer to call\n         ;; (yin.repl.publication).  A store that declares no durable HEAD\n         ;; has no medium, and its round settles locally exactly as an\n         ;; ephemeral composition always has; a composition that wants to\n         ;; observe an ephemeral round injects the media itself.\n         media (or publication-media\n                   (when-let [head-fn (:head-fn index-store)]\n                     (publication/local-media\n                       {:head-fn head-fn\n                        :durability :persistent})))\n         ;; `:media` is the engine's view of the pair -- the request side\n         ;; it appends to, the result side it reads and its cursor -- with\n         ;; the composition's durable HEAD writer stripped off it, so no\n         ;; callback hook sits inside the indexer.  `:local-service` is\n         ;; that stripped half, the medium with its writer, which the\n         ;; round boundary services (`serve-publication`); a composition\n         ;; with transport of its own injects a medium with no `:local`,\n         ;; has no service here, and services the request side itself.\n         publication {:publication-policy publication-policy\n                      :media (some-> media publication/engine-media)\n                      :local-service (when (:local media) media)}]\n     (merge\n       (update (make-session vm-type output-stream\n                             (merge (selected-primitives frontends lang)\n                                    primitives)\n                             shell-token\n                             index-store link-source publication\n                             host-modules)\n               :indexer index/rehydrate recovery)\n       {:lang lang\n        :frontends (or frontends frontend/empty-catalog)\n        :vm-type vm-type\n        :extra-primitives primitives\n        :output-stream output-stream\n        :output-cursor output-cursor\n        :ledger {:output :untried}\n        :shell-token shell-token\n        :index-store index-store\n        :index-store-spec index-store-spec\n        :publication publication\n        :host-modules (or host-modules {})\n        :registered-ops (query/registered-ops host-modules)\n        :index-recovery (or recovery {:manifest nil :datoms nil})\n        :round 0\n        :ingress-loss? false\n        :last-value nil\n        :last-value-2 nil\n        :last-value-3 nil\n        :pending-input nil\n        :link-source link-source\n        :admission admission\n        :initial-admission admission\n        :link-policy (checked-link-policy link-policy)\n        :pending-run nil\n        :custody custody\n        :running? true}))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition's explicit engine operations\n;; (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 4)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn pending-publication\n  \"The oldest publication request this shell has emitted and no matching\n   result has settled, or nil.  A composition reads it to know what it\n   still owes the engine before it may report the round settled.\"\n  [state]\n(defn- eval-program\n  \"Evaluate one frontend program — the map AST the compilers emit or a\n   datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n   projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n   declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the code and AST indexers and then\n   the evaluator only when a program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n   batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n   input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n   is appended.\n\n   The observers recover across a gap on their own, but the shell reads the\n   gap counts around the round: an increase on any medium means one or more\n   batches were never run, so resuming as though execution were complete\n   would report a result built on programs the VM never saw.  The loss is\n   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`.\n\n   A completed program's lexical environment does not outlive it: the VM's\n   environment is restored to the one the round began with, as `vm/eval`\n   does.  A round that throws is consumed by `consume-failed-round`.\"\n  [state program]\n  (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n    [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n    (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n          tables-before (call-site-tables state')\n          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n        (let [expanded (try\n                         (run-expander-stage state')\n                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                                   :clj Exception\n                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n            failed\n            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n                  indexed (if (pos? forwarded)\n                            ;; commit evidence is captured BEFORE the\n                            ;; index stage runs: the published programs\n                            ;; and indexer as they stood, so the recorder\n                            ;; pairs only what this round commits\n                            (let [evidence\n                                  {:programs-before\n                                   (indexed-program-roots (:indexer expanded))\n                                   :indexer-before (:indexer expanded)}]\n                              (-> expanded\n                                  run-index-stage\n                                  run-ast-index-stage\n                                  (assoc :call-site-commit-evidence evidence)\n                                  ;; cc3 r2 item 4: this round's\n                                  ;; provenance claims — the roots the\n                                  ;; expander newly retained under\n                                  ;; exactly one admission — ride the\n                                  ;; state into the evaluator stage,\n                                  ;; whose loader wrapper retains each\n                                  ;; claimed packet's provenance\n                                  (assoc :call-site-round-claims\n                                         (let [new-entries\n                                               (into {}\n                                                     (remove\n                                                       (fn [[k _]]\n                                                         (contains?\n                                                           (or tables-before {})\n                                                           k)))\n                                                     (or (call-site-tables\n                                                           expanded)\n                                                         {}))\n                                               by-root\n                                               (group-by (fn [[k _]]\n                                                           (second k))\n                                                         new-entries)]\n                                           (into {}\n                                                 (keep (fn [[root entries]]\n                                                         (when (= 1 (count entries))\n                                                           [root (first (ffirst entries))])))\n                                                 by-root)))\n                                  ((fn [s]\n                                     (record-call-site-admissions\n                                       tables-before s)))))\n                            expanded)]\n              (with-index-notice\n                (cond\n                  (> (ingress-gaps indexed) (ingress-gaps state'))\n                  [(assoc indexed :ingress-loss? true)\n                   (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n\n                  (pos? forwarded) (run-evaluation state indexed)\n\n                  :else [(assoc indexed :vm (:vm state))\n                         (format-expansion-errors errors)])\n                (when (pos? forwarded)\n                  [(index/notice (:indexer expanded) (:indexer indexed))\n                   (ast-index/notice (:ast-indexer indexed))])))))))))\n\n\n(defn- installed-text\n  \"The languages and ids `catalog` holds, for a refused selection to name:\n   a name that is neither is a typo, not a missing frontend.\"\n  [catalog]\n  (let [entries (:yang.frontend/entries catalog)\n        listed (fn [xs] (str/join \" \" (map pr-str (sort (distinct xs)))))]\n    (str \"installed: \"\n         (listed (map (comp :yang.frontend/language :manifest) (vals entries)))\n         \" (ids \" (listed (map first (keys entries))) \")\")))\n\n\n(defn- select-frontend\n  \"Select the frontend `lang` names in `catalog`: a qualified id selects\n   by id (ambiguous when several revisions are installed), `[id revision]`\n   pins one revision; anything else is refused — the selector is the\n   frontend id, never a language keyword.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2484,2636p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2790,2866p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '411,452p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '628,650p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2484,2636p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '2790,2866p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '411,452p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; sed -n '628,650p' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- rebuild-session\n  \"Replace the VM, the expander, and their media, attachments, and\n   observers.  The value history is cleared with them: a closure in `*1`\n   names a code segment the old VM held, which the new one does not.  The\n   new expander holds only the standard forms.  A require still pending\n   on the old VM is dropped with it: its link pair is the session's, and\n   the new session answers from its own.\n\n   Over a durable store the code index is not the session's to drop: the\n   new indexer continues the old one's log, entity allocation, and\n   published manifest (`yin.repl.index/carry-over`), so a rebuild never\n   resets `t`.  Over the memory store it starts empty, as it always has.\"\n  [state vm-type]\n  (merge state\n         (cond-> (make-session vm-type (:output-stream state)\n                               (merge (selected-primitives (:frontends state)\n                                                           (:lang state))\n                                      (:extra-primitives state))\n                               (:shell-token state)\n                               (:index-store state)\n                               (:link-source state)\n                               (cond-> (:publication state)\n                                 (get-in state [:indexer :publication-media])\n                                 (assoc :media\n                                        (get-in state\n                                                [:indexer :publication-media])))\n                               (:host-modules state))\n           (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n           (update :indexer index/carry-over (:indexer state)))\n         {:vm-type vm-type\n          :ingress-loss? false\n          :last-value nil\n          :last-value-2 nil\n          :last-value-3 nil\n          :frontend-session nil\n          :pending-run nil}))\n\n\n(defn- configure-admission\n  \"Apply session configuration to the linker, retaining its live state.\"\n  [state admission]\n  (let [linker (link/reconfigure (:linker state) admission)]\n    (assoc state :admission admission :linker linker\n           :link-source (:source linker))))\n\n\n(defn- trust-command\n  [state command args]\n  (try\n    (let [p (first args)]\n      (when-not (and (= 1 (count args)) (string? p)\n                     (str/starts-with? p \"ed25519:\"))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Expected one ed25519:<64 hex> principal id\" {})))\n      (let [p (config/parse-trust p)\n            admission (if (= :external (:admission state))\n                        {} (:admission state))]\n        (if (and (= command 'untrust)\n                 (contains? (:own (:link-source state)) p))\n          [state (str \"Own principal \" p \" is always trusted\")]\n          [(configure-admission\n             state (update admission :trusted\n                           (fn [trusted]\n                             ((if (= command 'trust) conj disj)\n                              (set trusted) p))))\n           (if (nil? (:admission (:link-source state)))\n             (str \"Recorded \" (if (= command 'trust) \"trust\" \"untrust\")\n                  \" for \" p \"; unused while admission is external\")\n             (str (if (= command 'trust) \"Trusted \" \"Untrusted \") p))])))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n      [state (str \"Error: \" (ex-message e))])))\n\n\n(declare repl-state)\n\n\n(defn handle-command\n  \"Answer one shell command.  Unsupported arguments are answered as text, not\n   thrown, so a mistyped command cannot end a step.\"\n  [state form]\n  (let [[command & args] form]\n    (case command\n      vm (let [vm-type (first args)]\n           (if (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n             [(rebuild-session state vm-type)\n              (str \"Switched to \" (get vm-labels vm-type)\n                   (if (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n                     \" (VM store cleared; durable code index kept)\"\n                     \" (store cleared)\"))]\n             [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL VM type \" (pr-str vm-type)\n                         \"; supported: \"\n                         (pr-str (vec (keys vm-constructors))))]))\n      lang (let [lang (first args)]\n             (if (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) lang))\n               [(switch-lang state lang)\n                (str \"Switched to \" lang)]\n               [state (str \"Error: unavailable-parser: Yin REPL language \"\n                           (pr-str lang) \" is not in the frontend catalog; \"\n                           (installed-text (:frontends state)))]))\n      compile [state (render-compile-output\n                       state\n                       (compile-command-ast state (first args)))]\n      trust (trust-command state command args)\n      untrust (trust-command state command args)\n      trusted [state (str \"Own: \" (pr-str (first (:own (:link-source state))))\n                          \"\\nTrusted: \"\n                          (pr-str (vec (sort (:trusted (:admission state))))))]\n      reset [(rebuild-session\n               (configure-admission state (:initial-admission state))\n               (:vm-type state))\n             (str (get vm-labels (:vm-type state)) \" reset\")]\n      abandon (abandon-pending state)\n      help [state help-text]\n      repl-state [state (format-value (repl-state state))]\n      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n      host [state host-text]\n      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n\n\n(defn- eval-compiled\n  \"Evaluate a program `compile-input` or `compile-source` lowered.  What\n   its lowering left (`::frontend`: the session and the `:render` hook) is\n   staged on the round and committed only where the round's VM state\n   survives: when the program halts, now or when its parked require\n   completes (`finalize-eval`).  A round that fails, rolls back, or is\n   abandoned keeps the shell's previous `:frontend-session`.\"\n  [state ast]\n  (let [staged (::frontend (meta ast))\n        [state' text] (eval-program (cond-> state\n                                      staged (assoc ::frontend staged))\n                                    ast)]\n    [(dissoc state' ::frontend) text]))\n\n\n(defn- eval-parsed*\n  \"The parse dispatch of one line, against a shell with no require to\n   re-check.\"\n  [state trimmed parsed]\n  (try\n    (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n          form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n      (cond\n        (and form (command-form? form)) (handle-command state form)\n        (and form (datom-stream? form)) (eval-program state (vec form))\n        (and form (ast-map? form)) (eval-program state form)\n        forms (eval-compiled state (compile-input state trimmed forms))\n        (forms-input? state) [state (format-error (:error parsed))]\n        :else (eval-compiled state (compile-source state trimmed))))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n      (let [[state' output-text] (drain-output state)]\n        [state' (str output-text (format-error error))]))))\n\n\n  [state trimmed parsed]\n  (recheck-pending* state {:trimmed trimmed, :parsed parsed} false))\n\n\n(defn- command-line?\n  [parsed]\n  (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n        form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n    (and form (command-form? form))))\n\n\n(defn- eval-parsed\n  [state trimmed parsed]\n  (if (and (:pending-run state) (not (command-line? parsed)))\n    ;; A require is still pending: re-check it first.  While it stays\n    ;; pending the line is retained -- the parked VM owns the store a new\n    ;; evaluation would fork -- and it evaluates, in typing order and\n    ;; exactly once, when the link completes.\n    (resume-pending state trimmed parsed)\n    (eval-parsed* state trimmed parsed)))\n\n\n(defn- input-probe\n  \"The completeness probe of the session's frontend, or nil when it has\n   none or none is installed (the compile then reports it).\"\n  [state]\n  (:probe (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) (:lang state)))))\n\n\n(defn eval-input\n  \"Evaluate one input line locally, returning `[state text]`.\n\n   Input that is not yet a whole submission is retained as `:pending-input`\n   and produces no text: for a frontend with a `:probe` the probe decides\n   and the line is kept verbatim (whitespace can be inside a string);\n   otherwise the brackets must balance.  Nothing here is asynchronous: the\n   driver, not this namespace, decides when the next step happens.\"\n  [state line]\n  (let [probe (input-probe state)\n        pending (or (:pending-input state) \"\")\n        line (if probe line (str/trim line))\n        combined (if (str/blank? pending)\n                   line\n                   (str pending \"\\n\" line))]\n    (cond\n      (and probe (str/blank? combined))\n      [(assoc state :pending-input nil) \"\"]\n\n      (if probe\n        (= :incomplete (probe combined))\n        (pos? (bracket-balance combined)))\n      [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n\n      :else\n      (let [state' (assoc state :pending-input nil)\n            parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                                  :clj Exception\n                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n                          {:error error}))]\n        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n\n\n(defn repl-state\n  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n\n   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n   operation.\n   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n   :stack (fn [vm packet]\n            (append-stack-image\n              vm\n              (:image (derive/stack-image (packet->vector packet)))))\n   :register (fn [vm packet]\n               (append-register-image\n                 vm\n                 (derive/register-image (packet->vector packet))))})\n\n\n(def command-heads\n  \"Commands this shell answers.  `connect` and `disconnect` belong to the\n   driver, which owns the RPC client; `telemetry` is answered only to say that\n   this REPL slice does not have it.\"\n  #{'vm 'lang 'compile 'reset 'help 'repl-state 'quit 'telemetry 'abandon\n    'trust 'untrust 'trusted 'host})\n\n\n(def help-text\n  (str \"Commands:\\n\"\n       \"  (vm :ast-walker | :semantic | :stack | :register)\\n\"\n       \"  (lang :yang/clojure | :yang/python | :yang/php)\\n\"\n       \"  (compile expr)\\n\"\n       \"  (reset)\\n\"\n       \"  (trust \\\"ed25519:<64 hex>\\\") / (untrust \\\"ed25519:<64 hex>\\\")\\n\"\n       \"  (trusted)  - own principal and trusted set\\n\"\n       \"  (connect \\\"daostream:ws://host:port\\\")\\n\"\n       \"  (disconnect)\\n\"\n       \"  (require (quote m))  - link module m; a composition that serves\"\n       \" remote content may fetch m's code from peers, and the require stays\"\n       \" pending until it has\\n\"\n       \"  (abandon)  - give up a (require ...) that is still pending\\n\"\n       \"  (require (quote yin.link)), then (yin.link/publish (quote m)\"\n       \" (quote [f]))  - publish module m exporting f from this session's\"\n       \" indexed code under the session's publisher principal, and\"\n       \" (yin.link/names)\"\n       \"  - the names this node resolves\\n\"\n       \"  (require (quote yin.head)), then (yin.head/heads)  - each followed\"\n       \" principal's installed head, and (yin.head/moved)  - the linked\"\n       \" names a newer head moved\\n\"\n       \"  (host)  - the runtime this REPL runs on\\n\"\n       \"  (repl-state)\\n\"\n  ([value] (format-value value nil))\n  ([value namer]\n   (rendered-text (quote-symbols namer false value))))\n\n\n(defn format-error\n  [error]\n  (str \"Error: \"\n       #?(:cljd (or (ex-message error) (str error))\n          :cljs (or (ex-message error) (.-message error) (str error))\n          :clj (or (ex-message error) (str error)))))\n\n\n(defn- print-arg\n  [value]\n  (if (string? value) value (format-value value)))\n\n\n(defn- print-text\n  [args]\n  (str/join \" \" (map print-arg args)))\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1163,1225p' test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc; sed -n '280,353p' test/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn step|remote-routed\\\\?|result|driver/step' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc | tail -15; rg -n 'realpath|locked by|canonical' src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc; rg -n 'transactions|defn recover' src/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc; rg -n 'rg .*d(h|\\\\[)|Gate A' docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1163,1225p' test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc; sed -n '280,353p' test/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn step|remote-routed\\\\?|result|driver/step' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc | tail -15; rg -n 'realpath|locked by|canonical' src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc; rg -n 'transactions|defn recover' src/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc; rg -n 'rg .*d(h|\\\\[)|Gate A' docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"\n(def ^:private require-line\n  \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\")\n\n\n(defn- q-line\n  [query & more]\n  (str \"(dao.space.query/q (quote \" (pr-str query) \")\"\n       (apply str (map #(str \" \" %) more))\n       \")\"))\n\n\n(defn- evaluate\n  [state lines]\n  (reduce (fn [[state texts] line]\n            (let [[state' text] (repl/eval-input state line)]\n              [state' (conj texts text)]))\n          [state []]\n          lines))\n\n\n(defn- provenance-line\n  \"A history-view query for the session token and t of the literal\n   `value` — a constant only one def carries.  It sits inside the quoted\n   query, never as an input, so the calling line's own literals (every\n   program is indexed, the calling one included) cannot match it.\"\n  [value]\n  (q-line [:find '?s '?t\n           :where ['?e :yin/value value '?t '?m]\n           ['?m :yin.repl/session '?s '?t1 '?m1]]\n          \"{:view :history}\"))\n\n\n(defn- provenance\n  \"The `[token t]` pairs a provenance answer's text names.\"\n  [text]\n  (set (map (fn [[_ token t]] [token (read-edn t)])\n            (re-seq #\"\\[\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\" (\\d+)\\]\" (str text)))))\n\n\n(defn- local-datoms\n  \"Every datom of the indexer's retained transaction log.\"\n  [state]\n  (mapcat :datoms (transactions state)))\n\n\n(defn- ids-of\n  \"The entity and metadata-entity ids a datom set uses.\"\n  [datoms]\n  (into #{}\n        (comp (mapcat (fn [[e _a _v _t m]] [e m]))\n              (filter #(and (integer? %) (<= datom/first-user-id %))))\n        datoms))\n\n\n(deftest a-restarted-durable-shell-answers-q-with-the-previous-runs-facts\n  (let [dir (temp-dir)\n        spec {:type :file :dir dir}]\n    (try\n      (let [[first-run _] (evaluate (repl.frontends/create-state {:index-store-spec spec})\n                                    [\"(def alpha 1001)\"])\n            first-token (:shell-token first-run)\n            first-datoms (set (local-datoms first-run))\n;; The requests/answers round trip\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- eval!\n  \"Append one eval request directly onto the endpoint's requests medium,\n   as the mirror's own `:dao.stream/append!` answer would once a\n   reflection's write reaches it -- the wire and its answering are\n   dao.stream.remote-channel's own concern, already proven by its test\n   suite.\"\n  [endpoint id source]\n  (stream/append! (:requests endpoint) (rpc/request-value id :op/eval [source])))\n\n\n(defn- answers-since\n  \"Every answer appended after `cursor`, oldest first, as [answers\n   next-cursor].\"\n  [endpoint cursor]\n  (loop [cursor cursor acc []]\n    (let [r (stream/next (:answers endpoint) cursor)]\n      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n        [acc cursor]))))\n\n\n(deftest a-request-evaluates-against-the-shared-shell-and-answers-once\n  (let [{:keys [endpoint]} (endpoint!)\n        endpoint (serve/step endpoint 1)\n        answers-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor (:answers endpoint)\n                                                          stream/anchor-oldest))]\n    (eval! endpoint 7 \"(+ 1 2)\")\n    (let [endpoint (serve/step endpoint 2)\n          [answers _cursor] (answers-since endpoint answers-cursor)]\n      (is (= [(rpc/success-answer 7 \"3\")] answers)))))\n\n\n(deftest the-shared-shell-is-threaded-serially-across-requests\n  (let [{:keys [endpoint]} (endpoint!)\n        endpoint (serve/step endpoint 1)\n        answers-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor (:answers endpoint)\n                                                          stream/anchor-oldest))]\n    (eval! endpoint 1 \"(def x 41)\")\n    (let [endpoint (serve/step endpoint 2)]\n      (eval! endpoint 2 \"(+ x 1)\")\n      (let [endpoint (serve/step endpoint 3)\n            [answers _cursor] (answers-since endpoint answers-cursor)]\n        (is (= [(rpc/success-answer 1 \"41\") (rpc/success-answer 2 \"42\")]\n               answers))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-served-host-function-renders-as-the-local-marker\n  (let [{:keys [endpoint]} (endpoint!)\n        endpoint (serve/step endpoint 1)\n        answers-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor (:answers endpoint)\n                                                          stream/anchor-oldest))\n        lines [\"+\" \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\" \"dao.space.query/q\"]\n        local (second (reduce (fn [[state texts] line]\n                                (let [[state' text] (repl/eval-input state line)]\n                                  [state' (conj texts text)]))\n                              [(repl.frontends/create-state) []]\n                              lines))\n        endpoint (reduce (fn [endpoint [i line]]\n                           (eval! endpoint i line)\n                           (serve/step endpoint (+ 2 i)))\n                         endpoint\n                         (map-indexed vector lines))\n        [answers _cursor] (answers-since endpoint answers-cursor)]\n    (is (= \"{:type :host-fn, :name '+}\" (first local)))\n    (is (= \"{:type :host-fn, :name 'dao.space.query/q}\" (last local)))\n    (is (= (map-indexed rpc/success-answer local) answers)\n        \"a served session renders every host function as a local one does\")\n    (is (not-any? #(str/includes? % \"#object[\") (map :dao.stream.apply/ok answers)))))\n\n\n(deftest an-unknown-operation-is-a-portable-error-not-a-thrown-handler\n327:      (connect-failure state result)\n335:          (assoc :connection (get result connect/connection-key))\n336:          (attach-remote (adapter/state (get result connect/client-key)))\n375:      (and (remote-routed? state) (not (remote-terminal state)))\n398:  (let [result (adapter/submit-input (:adapter state) line)\n399:        state (assoc state :adapter (:yin.repl.adapter/state result))]\n400:    (case (:yin.repl.adapter/outcome result)\n403:             :outstanding (get-in result [:yin.repl.adapter/rpc-result\n421:                        (name (:yin.repl.adapter/outcome result))))))))\n448:        (publish :yin.repl.driver/result\n451:      (and (remote-routed? state) (not command))\n527:      (let [result (adapter/poll-responses (:adapter state) response-budget)]\n529:                                       (:yin.repl.adapter/state result)))))))\n552:  (if (and (remote-routed? state)\n562:  (if (and (remote-routed? state)\n48:   nothing but the canonical paths of the directories this process\n71:  (throw (ex-info (str dir \" is locked by another process\")\n164:             (throw (ex-info (str dir \" is locked by another process\"\n176:  ;; (see the namespace docstring): the canonical paths of the durable\n181:(defn- canonical-dir\n182:  \"The directory's one canonical path: the key of this process's own\n186:     :jolt (posix-file/realpath dir)\n188:     :cljs (.realpathSync ^js (js/require \"fs\") dir)))\n257:   (let [key (canonical-dir dir)]\n67:section 10. Gate A requires zero storage-implementation references in the\n341:row must reach its disposition before Gate A can pass. A literal search\n554:### Gate A — zero storage-implementation references\n559:if rg --hidden --no-ignore -n -F -- 'dao.jing.dht' \\\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
