{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' test/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc; sed -n '351,400p;565,650p' src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc; rg -n 'banner-lines|close-store\"'!|admitting'\"\\\\?' src/cljc/yin/{repl,shell}/main.cljc; rg -n 'defn.*(rehydrate|pending-publications)|call-provenance-handles|eval-program' src/cljc/yin/repl{.cljc,/index.cljc}; rg -n 'test.*(node|cljd|jolt)|jolt.*test' Makefile bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn | head -75\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.serve-test\n  \"The server side of the DaoStream Yin REPL, over the request-and-response\n   service of docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md section 5.\n\n   The host is the in-process loopback net (yin.repl.net-fixture): its\n   `:bind!` and `:unbind!` deposit lifecycle data, and a real\n   `yin.repl.connect` client attaches through its `:connect!`, so the\n   endpoint's sessions, drain and stop are observed from a client on every\n   host.  Nothing here binds a port.  The requests/answers interpreter is\n   tested at the level serve.cljc itself owns -- the shared buffers\n   `serve!` composes -- since the wire and the mirror answering it are\n   dao.stream.remote-channel's own, already proven by its test suite; the\n   demo REPL flow over a real socket is proven end to end in\n   yin.repl.serve-connect-wire-test (JVM).\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n            [yin.repl.net-fixture :as fixture]\n            [yin.repl.serve :as serve]\n            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; An injected host listener\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- endpoint!\n  ([] (endpoint! {}))\n  ([extra]\n   (let [h (fixture/host)]\n     {:host h\n      :endpoint (serve/serve! (merge {:bind-port 8080\n                                      :host (:adapter h)}\n                                     extra))})))\n\n\n(defn- texts\n  [endpoint]\n  (mapv :yin.repl.serve/text (first (serve/take-outbox endpoint))))\n\n\n(defn- tick\n  \"One server turn at `now` with the net pumped around it.\"\n  [h endpoint now]\n  (fixture/pump! h)\n  (let [endpoint (serve/step endpoint now)]\n    (fixture/pump! h)\n    endpoint))\n\n\n(defn- connect!\n  \"Open one client to the endpoint and drive both until its answers cursor\n   is minted.  Returns [endpoint client now].\"\n  [h endpoint now]\n  (let [c (fixture/open h (serve/url endpoint) now)]\n    (is (some? c) \"the client attached\")\n    (loop [endpoint endpoint now now left 50]\n      (let [endpoint (tick h endpoint now)]\n        (fixture/client-step! c now)\n        (if (and (pos? left) (rpc/cursor-pending? @(:client c)))\n          (recur endpoint (inc now) (dec left))\n          [endpoint c (inc now)])))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Composition data ownership\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest serve-returns-immediately-with-its-media-and-channel-server\n  (let [{:keys [endpoint host]} (endpoint!)]\n    (is (some? (:server endpoint)))\n    (is (some? (:requests endpoint)))\n    (is (some? (:answers endpoint)))\n    (is (= \"/repl\" (:path endpoint)))\n    (is (= :starting (:status endpoint))\n        \"serve! claims nothing about a bind it has not observed\")\n    (is (= 1 (count @(:bound host))))\n    (is (nil? (:ws-endpoint endpoint)) \"no transport internals above the boundary\")\n    (is (nil? (:acceptor endpoint)) \"no transport internals above the boundary\")\n    (let [endpoint (serve/step endpoint 1)]\n      (is (= :running (:status endpoint)))\n      (is (str/includes? (str/join \" \" (texts endpoint))\n                         \"Serving daostream:ws://127.0.0.1:8080/repl\")))))\n\n\n      (not (and (string? url)\n                (or (empty? opts)\n                    (and (= 2 (count opts)) (= :codec (first opts))))\n                codec))\n      (publish state :yin.repl.driver/notice connect-usage)\n\n      (and (:connection state)\n           (= url (:url (:connection state)))\n           (connect/reattachable? (:connection state) (rpc-client state)))\n      (reattach state url (when (seq opts) codec))\n\n      ;; The operator's own disconnection is in flight: the terminal fact has\n      ;; not landed yet, so there is nothing to reattach to and nothing to\n      ;; refuse.  Composing a second boundary here would abandon the first.\n      ;; Once a terminal has landed the boundary has said everything it will\n      ;; ever say, so this must not answer for a non-reattachable one — that\n      ;; would trap the operator on a connection nothing can revive.\n      (and (:connection state)\n           (connect/operator-detached? (:connection state))\n           (nil? (remote-terminal state)))\n      (publish state :yin.repl.driver/notice\n               (str \"Still disconnecting from \" (:url (:connection state))\n                    \"; (connect …) reattaches once the boundary reports it\"))\n\n      (and (remote-routed? state) (not (remote-terminal state)))\n      (publish state :yin.repl.driver/notice\n               (str \"Already connected to \"\n                    (or (:url (:connection state)) \"the remote shell\")\n                    \"; (disconnect) first\"))\n\n      :else (open-connection state url codec))))\n\n\n(defn- queue-line\n  [state line]\n  (update state :queued conj line))\n\n\n(defn- requeue-line\n  [state line]\n  (update state :queued #(into [line] %)))\n\n\n(defn- submit-remote\n  \"Offer `line` to RPC once.  `hold` puts the line back where it came from\n   when RPC refuses to send before its response cursor is minted.\"\n  [state line hold]\n  (let [result (adapter/submit-input (:adapter state) line)\n        state (assoc state :adapter (:yin.repl.adapter/state result))]\n    (case (:yin.repl.adapter/outcome result)\n           (not (:outstanding state))\n           (not (:retrying state))\n           (not (remote-unsent? state)))\n    (let [[line & rest-lines] (:queued state)]\n      (-> state\n          (assoc :queued (vec rest-lines))\n          (submit-remote line requeue-line)))\n    state))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The step\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn repl-step\n  \"Advance the REPL once.  Called by exactly one ticker per host; never loops on\n   `:dao.stream/blocked`.  `now` is the host's clock reading, recorded but not\n   waited on: this layer has no deadline of its own.\"\n  [state now]\n  (let [state (assoc state :last-tick now)\n        state (retry-unsent state)\n        ;; Completions and lifecycle are observed before this tick's lines are\n        ;; handled, so a `(connect …)` typed in the same tick as the drop that\n        ;; makes it legal sees the terminal fact rather than being told the\n        ;; shell is already connected.\n        state (poll-remote state now)\n        state (observe-connection state)\n        [state lines] (drain-input state)\n        state (reduce handle-line state lines)]\n    (release-queue state)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc:56:          :close-store! shell.store/close!\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc:65:          :admitting? shell.dht/admitting?\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:250:    (try ((or (:close-store! composition) store/close!)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:409:(defn- composition-admitting?\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:415:  (if-some [admitting? (:admitting? (:composition state))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:416:    (boolean (admitting? (session-of state)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:714:  ((or (:close-store! (:composition state)) store/close!)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:726:   `:banner-lines` hook — what it will share, and what it will refuse —\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:751:     (:banner-lines composition)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:752:     (into ((:banner-lines composition) opts))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:854:      (not (composition-admitting? state))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:241:   lookup key `call-provenance-handles` carries on the session state —\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:306:(defn call-provenance-handles\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:313:  (:call-provenance-handles state))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:322:   `call-provenance-handles`; an unclaimed admission appears in\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1258:(defn pending-publications\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1634:   index: `eval-program` captures the round's\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1714:        ;; out (`call-provenance-handles`). Unclaimed packets retain\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1771:                           (update :call-provenance-handles merge @handles)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1781:      (seq @handles) (update :call-provenance-handles merge @handles)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2223:                                  (seq (:call-provenance-handles @latest))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2224:                                  (update :call-provenance-handles\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2226:                                          (:call-provenance-handles @latest))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2244:(defn- eval-program\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2612:        [state' text] (eval-program (cond-> state\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2627:        (and form (datom-stream? form)) (eval-program state (vec form))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2628:        (and form (ast-map? form)) (eval-program state form)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:267:(defn rehydrate\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc:665:(defn pending-publications\nrg: Makefile: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nshadow-cljs.edn:18:          :test {:target :node-test\nbb.edn:8:  {:doc \"J6f Autobahn conformance: starts the testee and the Dockerized pinned suite, waits for the READY barrier, runs harness.py per role, collects results/, and shuts both sides down. Usage: bb autobahn:jolt <role> <agent>\"\nbb.edn:21:  test:jolt-bootstrap-neg\nbb.edn:24:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\" \"--test-negative\")))}\nbb.edn:58:  test:jolt-j5\nbb.edn:130:  test:jolt-host\nbb.edn:131:  {:doc \"J1: the dao.host oracle (conformance, bytes, float, text tests) under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj; counts per namespace, nonzero exit on any failure, error or load failure (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:134:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.host.conformance-test dao.host.bytes-test dao.host.float-test dao.host.text-test\")))}\nbb.edn:141:  {:doc \"J2: staged load probe of the J2 load order under -M:jolt:jolt-test, one namespace per process (load-ok / first failing require / first unresolved symbol / first load-time error + the loaded-libs delta asserting dao.stream.transit absent); logs under build/j2-logs/probe (src/dev/jolt_j2_probe.clj; needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:158:  test:jolt-shell\nbb.edn:163:  test:jolt-core\nbb.edn:164:  {:doc \"J2: every applicable pure suite (test/dao/host, jing, data, space, portable stream, yin/vm) under jolt, one namespace per process through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj, fast and ^:slow alike (Q3), nonzero exit on any failure; excluded suites are printed and recorded with reason/capability/owner\"\nbb.edn:168:  test:jolt-core:diag\nbb.edn:169:  {:doc \"J2 DIAGNOSTIC: test:jolt-core with the :jolt-diag alias added (the J1 corpus-loader stand-in for dao.jing.cbor-fixtures)\"\nbb.edn:173:  test:jolt-j2-jvm\nbb.edn:174:  {:doc \"J2: the JVM counts baseline — the sa