{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' src/jolt/dao/host/hash.jolt; rg -n 'native|BLAKE' src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj | head -25; ls -d /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/native/*/*(/N); ls -ld /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/antlr/php/js\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.host.hash\n  \"The jolt override of src/cljc/dao/host/hash.cljc (the :jolt alias puts\n   src/jolt first, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.2, §6.2,\n   §6.3): the same public entries, arities, docstrings and refusal data\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A).\n\n   P entries (§2.4): `blake3-bytes` and `sha256-bytes`. They take host\n   bytes (jolt's byte array) and return fresh host bytes representing the\n   32-byte digest (256 bits). They leave their arguments unmodified.\n\n   Both are `:blocking` calls into native/jolt-crypto, which `bb\n   build:jolt-native` builds: BLAKE3 is the vendored upstream C reference,\n   SHA-256 the declared system libcrypto's EVP API. The input is copied into\n   caller-owned native memory (never a C string, so embedded NUL is data),\n   the digest is read back into a fresh jolt byte array, and the memory is\n   freed on every path: each native acquisition owns its own release,\n   established as soon as it is acquired (`with-native`), so a later\n   allocation or copy that fails still frees every earlier buffer, and each\n   free runs whether or not another failed.\n\n   Loading this namespace is the provenance gate (§6.3): it refuses, by\n   throwing, unless the wrapper writes this namespace's layout and reports\n   that every EVP entry resolved to exactly the library jolt-toolchain.edn\n   qualified for this platform (:native :libcrypto :qualified): the same\n   canonical real path (which the declared :path must also resolve to), the\n   same OpenSSL_version_num and the same file SHA-256, at no lower than\n   :min-version. An upgrade, a repointed link or a replaced file therefore\n   fails until requalified (the procedure is in jolt-toolchain.edn). No\n   digest is computed before that check passes; a missing library fails the\n   load.\n\n   String digesting is a table B portable composition over `dao.host.text`\n   and these byte primitives (`blake3`, `sha256`, `digest-string`,\n   `digest-bytes`), hosted in `dao.jing`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The native library and its provenance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private platform\n  ;; as yang.antlr.cst decides it: jolt's os.name/os.arch shim can answer\n  ;; nil, which reads as Linux and x86_64\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (or (System/getProperty \"os.name\") \"\"))\n        arch (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")]\n    (str (if (str/includes? os \"mac\") \"darwin\" \"linux\") \"-\"\n         (if (#{\"aarch64\" \"arm64\"} arch) \"arm64\" \"x86_64\"))))\n\n\n(def ^:private library\n  ;; the wrapper `bb build:jolt-native` builds, under the working directory\n  (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\") \"/build/native/\" platform\n       \"/jolt-crypto/lib/libjolt_crypto\"\n       (if (str/starts-with? platform \"darwin\") \".dylib\" \".so\")))\n\n\n(def ^:private libcrypto-declaration\n  (get-in (edn/read-string (slurp (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\")\n                                       \"/jolt-toolchain.edn\")))\n          [:native :libcrypto]))\n\n\n(ffi/load-library library)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-layout-version \"jolt_crypto_layout_version\" [] :int)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-provenance \"jolt_crypto_provenance\" [:pointer :size_t] :int)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-blake3 \"jolt_crypto_blake3\"\n            [:pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-sha256 \"jolt_cr